  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "9eXWGZSkUsIquYDE9C+w9NV+Qkw=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:40.000Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Two primary documents shape BIM projects (DT BAU, 00:27:50):\n\n- **EIR / AIA** (Exchange Information Requirements) \u2014 requirements and best practices to be followed, **defined by the client**. Maintained as master templates, customized per project to define goals, milestones, and software requirements \u2014 specifically requiring IFC compatibility certified by buildingSMART (01:21:45).\n- **BEP / BAP** (BIM Execution Plan / BIM-Abwicklungsplan) \u2014 **discussed and agreed upon by all stakeholders**, dictating roles, processes, and necessary digital data.\n\nTogether they serve as the regulatory framework for managing stakeholder needs and controlling document access, visibility, and editing permissions (02:01:43). The BEP is created iteratively through continuous stakeholder communication, not solitary authoring (01:25:02) \u2014 in IPD projects it is agreed collectively, contrasting with traditional projects that suffer from conflicts.\n\nThese document types are the natural first candidates for a Powerhouse project-management document model in construction \u2014 Plannerly's document types (EIR, BEP) are the explicit inspiration for the dtbau demo's Source 3.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-14T18:11:40.708749+00:00"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-14T18:11:40.000Z"
    }
  },
